WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:09.418
In this video you’ll check your map the way your team will see it, then publish it

2
00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:10.649
so they can use it.

3
00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:13.937
Open your map from the Maps page.

4
00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:18.089
Everything you do in the editor saves as a draft.

5
00:00:18.089 --> 00:00:21.335
Your team doesn’t see it until you publish.

6
00:00:21.335 --> 00:00:24.656
The Publish button shows where things stand.

7
00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:31.612
First, choose Preview. This is exactly what your employees will see.

8
00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:34.364
Try it the way they would.

9
00:00:34.364 --> 00:00:39.669
Search for a space, like 1B5, and the map shows where it is.

10
00:00:40.122 --> 00:00:42.964
Check the other floors with the tabs at the bottom.

11
00:00:43.416 --> 00:00:48.716
If something needs fixing, choose Back to editing.

12
00:00:49.168 --> 00:00:52.292
When it looks right, choose Publish.

13
00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:55.069
Your team now sees this version.

14
00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:59.560
If you change the map later, the button says Publish changes.

15
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:04.458
Your team keeps seeing the last published version until you publish again.

16
00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:09.710
Choose Publish changes when you’re ready.

17
00:01:10.162 --> 00:01:14.103
Back on the Maps page, the map shows as published.

18
00:01:14.555 --> 00:01:20.335
Each site holds up to five maps, and two of them can be published at a time.

19
00:01:20.335 --> 00:01:24.443
For example, your everyday layout and an event layout.
